{
  "$defs": {
    "AssumptionDerivation": {
      "description": "HOW one assumption axis was modeled: a one-sentence analyst method + the reference frame.\n``references`` MAY be empty \u2014 a pure-judgment method honestly stated beats a fabricated\nreference; a blank method is refused like a blank reason.\n\nA method sentence is DRAFTED with the run and RATIFIED by the human at review. ``ratified_by``\n/``ratified`` record that second act, so a reviewer can tell a sentence the analyst stood\nbehind from one that merely shipped with the run. Absent = not yet ratified (the honest\ndefault); the machine never sets them.",
      "properties": {
        "method": {
          "title": "Method",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "references": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/RefPoint"
          },
          "title": "References",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "ratified_by": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Ratified By"
        },
        "ratified": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Ratified"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "method"
      ],
      "title": "AssumptionDerivation",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DatedTrigger": {
      "description": "(catalyst calendar, ratified 2026-07-24) An ANALYST-owned re-underwrite trigger with a\ndeadline \u2014 the dated form of a ``reunderwrite_triggers`` entry (\"Quest stalling two more\nquarters\" \u2192 the print that closes the window). ANALYST-TYPED ONLY: the machine never invents a\ntrigger or its date. The calendar renders these with the TRIGGER-DEADLINE basis; the monitor\nflags a passed deadline as \"re-underwrite due\" (a flag, never a machine action).",
      "properties": {
        "trigger": {
          "title": "Trigger",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "deadline": {
          "title": "Deadline",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "basis": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Basis",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "trigger",
        "deadline"
      ],
      "title": "DatedTrigger",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Fact": {
      "description": "One source-bound input. ``basis`` names WHAT the number is; ``source`` names WHERE it came\nfrom (form + accession + statement line) so the human can verify rather than trust.",
      "properties": {
        "value": {
          "title": "Value",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "unit": {
          "title": "Unit",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "basis": {
          "title": "Basis",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source": {
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "value",
        "unit",
        "basis",
        "source"
      ],
      "title": "Fact",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RefPoint": {
      "description": "One source-bound REFERENCE value an assumption was modeled against (a history median, an\nanchor, a floor, a peak). ``label`` names what it is (the ``basis`` role); recorded in\ndisplay-natural units (``4.06`` + ``\"%\"``, ``6.56`` + ``\"x\"``) \u2014 no consumer re-scales it.",
      "properties": {
        "label": {
          "title": "Label",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "value": {
          "title": "Value",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "unit": {
          "title": "Unit",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source": {
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "label",
        "value",
        "unit",
        "source"
      ],
      "title": "RefPoint",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RefreshEntry": {
      "description": "(record legibility, 2026-07-27) ONE machine data/spot refresh \u2014 what changed, old \u2192 new.\n\nTHE POINT: a machine refresh is not an amendment to anyone's reasoning, and putting it in the\nsealed rationale made the audit trail read like argument. SMPL's 88-word \"machine refresh on\ncurrent data\" tag is the specimen: it changed two numbers and cost a fifth of the record's\nprose. Refreshes now land HERE \u2014 structured, greppable, and machine-written by\n``vinci scenario-refresh`` \u2014 while ``machine``-class tags are refused from the rationale\noutright (vinci/seal.py).\n\nAppend-only by convention: entries are added, never edited. This log is NOT sealed \u2014 it is\nmachine-generated fact, reproducible from the sources it names, not a record of judgment.",
      "properties": {
        "field": {
          "title": "Field",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "old": {
          "title": "Old",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "new": {
          "title": "New",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "date": {
          "title": "Date",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source": {
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "field",
        "old",
        "new",
        "date",
        "source"
      ],
      "title": "RefreshEntry",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Result": {
      "description": "Filled by the run. ``pass_fail`` records the bar test honestly \u2014 a FAIL is a result.",
      "properties": {
        "per_scenario": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ScenarioOutcome"
          },
          "title": "Per Scenario",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "survival": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/SurvivalBlock"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "hurdle": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Hurdle"
        },
        "reward": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Reward"
        },
        "risk": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Risk"
        },
        "ratio": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Ratio"
        },
        "ratio_undefined": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Ratio Undefined"
        },
        "bar": {
          "default": 2.0,
          "title": "Bar",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "pass_fail": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "enum": [
                "PASS",
                "FAIL",
                "UNDEFINED"
              ],
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Pass Fail"
        }
      },
      "title": "Result",
      "type": "object"
    },
